{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.InvolutionNumbers","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.InvolutionNumbers","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Sigma","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.End"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_involutions_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_involutions_five","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L257-L259","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_involutions_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_involutions_four","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L254-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_involutions_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_involutions_three","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L251-L253","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_involutions_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_involutions_two","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L248-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_involutions_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_involutions_one","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L245-L247","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_involutions_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_involutions_zero","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L242-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_involutions_eq_involutionNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_involutions_eq_involutionNumber","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L230-L235","doc":"**General count identity.** The number of involutions (self-inverse permutations)\nof `Fin n` equals `involutionNumber n`, for every `n`. Equivalently, `involutionNumber`\ncounts `∑_{λ ⊢ n} f^λ` by the Frobenius–Schur / RSK correspondence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_values","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L56-L60","doc":"First values: `1, 1, 2, 4, 10, 26` (A000085). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The defining two-term recurrence, as a rewrite lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_one","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.involutionNumber_zero","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.involutionNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.involutionNumber","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InvolutionNumbers.lean#L41-L47","doc":"The involution / telephone numbers `A000085`, defined by the two-term\nrecurrence `I(n) = I(n-1) + (n-1)·I(n-2)` (`I(0) = I(1) = 1`). At `q = 1` this is\n`∑_{λ ⊢ n} dim_q(λ)|_{q=1} = ∑_{λ ⊢ n} f^λ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}